    "interpretation": "The 100-step paired run is the steadier benefit estimate: LP session versus one-shot warm is about 22%; QP session versus cold is about 4-5%. The post-final QP path additionally verifies every accepted result, increasing absolute wall time. Cross-run absolute times are not a clean causal speed comparison because verification and host load changed.",
    "counter_notes": "The initial 12-step driver reported zero for cold LP iterations and refactorizations because it read dual telemetry, which the reference cold oracle does not expose. The final driver reads phase-one plus phase-two iterations and records cold LP refactorizations as null. KKT refactorizations count the initial numeric factorization plus rho updates; the symbolic cache skips only analysis, so numeric counts remain 100."
